A||||9||boutip||Found source of electrical burning smell !!||||10
Z||000000||boutip||11-10-1999||09:29 PM||||A couple of days ago I wrote in about an electrical smell and wisps of smoke coming from the vents inside the car and air intakes outside my 88 GT. With the help of the service manual I went digging to figure it out. When I pulled out the blower motor resistors from their mount I looked inside and found a mouse's nest consisting of leaves and everything else you could imagine wrapped around the resistors. That was the smell. And the leaves were charred up bigtime. I consider myself lucky at this point that the whole damn thing didn't catch fire and melt to the ground. I remember catching a mouse in my garage about a year ago and thinking nothing of it. I think I finally found his home. Thanks to the folks who replied to help me out.||||reg||10
Z||000001||fiero56||11-10-1999||09:49 PM||||A few years back I had that same problem, only mine was recurring. Had the same problems you described. I finally realized it was a mouse nest, pulled it out, everything was fine. Until the next morning, and the next... I finally ended up putting a screen over the opening for the vent.  Problem solved.  That little mouse was persistant though, every morning he had another nest in there, after four days of this I finally put up that screen, no more problems.<BR>I'd say your pretty lucky though, wouldn't be very fun to watch your car burn <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.  <BR>Then when the news came, they could do a "follow-up" on dormant Fieros flaring up after 11 years.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-10-1999).]||||reg||14
Z||000002||theogre||11-11-1999||12:58 AM||||I had a mouse nest in my 73 Ford Maverick,,,, took the easy way out..... cut a hole in the heater box to extract it.<P>you are lucky..... Can you say Toast? Good, I knew you could.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan||11-11-1999||11:01 AM|||| Homewrecker!||||reg||1
Z||000004||dogtired||11-11-1999||11:24 AM||||Every chance I get I will wreck those type of homes!<BR>I have a 63 corvette (yes I purchased it long before they even started making Fiero's) that was stored at my folks house in their garage. Rats got in the engine compartment on top of the motor (327 covered in rat crap) anyway they chewed the insualtion off the wires, what a mess. My point here is make sure they just left a mess in your car and didn't do a bunch of damage.<BR>Check it out.||||reg||8
Z||000005||Linx||11-12-1999||09:18 AM||||Heh heh...of course, none of the rodents would have had the opportunity <I>to build</I> if ya'll would drive your cars <I>a little more often</I>.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 11-12-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||11-12-1999||09:44 AM||||I drove my car everyday to school and back(ahh, high school years...), but that mouse would get a good head start on it by the time I came to start my car the next morning. Here's another one, anybody know what it sounds like to have a cat sleeping on your intake manifold when you start up in the morning? One of the worst sounds I've ever heard.  Happend when I went over to a friends house one morning, we took his car out... wasn't his cat though, don't know who's it was, but it took off through the woods.||||reg||1
Z||000007||BOILERMAKER||11-12-1999||11:07 AM||||I had one of those cat incidents one time.<P>THUMP...THUMP...THUMP...BREAK<P>Wasn't good for the radiator.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DJRice||11-12-1999||04:16 PM||||I saw a cat that ended up with three legs thanks to a nap under a hood.  I also accidentally killed one when I assumed he would move out of the way when I moved the car...Talking about looking death in the face...||||reg||1
Z||000009||Richard Parnell||11-12-1999||05:27 PM||||Years ago I was driving my mothers Volvo (yeah I know), I'd been going along for about 5-6 miles when I started hearing the most godawful noise like screaching and howling coming out from the engine compartment.  My passenger and I looked at one another like what the heck is that.  I thought the engine was getting ready to fall out, but it wasn't like any engine noise I'd ever heard.  I stopped the car and when we got out and opened up the hood a cat came flying out from the top of the engine, between the two of us and headed for the woods.  I  had never seen that cat before and never saw that cat again.  True story.||||reg||10
